.\" Manual page for rea2nbin
.TH REA2NBIN 1 "2026-05-22" "Neko" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rea2nbin \- convert a Nek5000 re2 mesh to Neko's nmsh format
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rea2nbin
.I re2-file
.RI [ nmsh-file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rea2nbin
reads a binary Nek5000 mesh in
.B .re2
format and writes the equivalent Neko native mesh in
.B .nmsh
format. It is part of the Neko contrib tools and is installed only when
Neko has been configured with
.BR --enable-contrib .
.PP
The tool is intentionally serial: it must be run on a single MPI rank and
will abort with an error if launched with more than one rank.
.PP
The legacy ASCII
.B .rea
format is no longer supported. Such files must first be converted to
.B .re2
using Nek5000's own tools (for example
.BR reatore2 )
before being passed to
.BR rea2nbin .
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I re2-file
Input mesh file. Must end in
.BR .re2 .
.TP
.I nmsh-file
Optional output file name. Must end in
.BR .nmsh .
When omitted, the output name is derived from
.I re2-file
by replacing the
.B .re2
suffix with
.BR .nmsh .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The mesh was converted successfully.
.TP
.B non-zero
An error occurred. Typical causes include an unsupported input suffix
(e.g. a legacy
.B .rea
file), an invalid output suffix, launching the tool on more than one rank,
or an I/O failure while reading or writing the mesh.
.SH EXAMPLES
Convert a mesh, letting
.B rea2nbin
choose the output name:
.PP
.RS
.B rea2nbin box.re2
.RE
.PP
This produces
.IR box.nmsh .
.PP
Convert a mesh with an explicit output name:
.PP
.RS
.B rea2nbin box.re2 cavity.nmsh
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR neko (1),
.BR prepart (1)
.PP
